Subject: [PATCH] AntiXray entity / hologram / drop occlusion hook

Extends the SourbyCraft RayTraceAntiXray port to entity broadcast:
when antixray.entity-raytrace.enabled = true, ChunkMap.TrackedEntity
consults EntityVisibilityCheck.isVisibleSync(player, entity) before
adding the player to the tracker's seenBy set.

Result: a mob, item drop, or hologram (TextDisplay / armor-stand with
custom name) sitting behind a wall stays client-invisible. Liquids
are handled by Paper's anticheat.anti-xray.fluid-obscures toggle and
need no NMS patch; the operator section in README documents this.

The check runs on the main thread (tracker update is already main-
thread per Spigot's AsyncCatcher.catchOp), so the per-call level.clip
cost is acceptable at the 1-in-N tracker cadence.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
index bec7ae2f9f5646fa9e1ddd06d37d75b8215c8715..c21ff9bc0da3e972c1f1ddc8c480f1a593fd6c4c 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
@@ -1380,6 +1380,12 @@ public class ChunkMap extends SimpleRegionStorage implements ChunkHolder.PlayerP
                     visibleToPlayer = false;
                 }
                 // CraftBukkit end
+                // SourbyCraft start - RayTraceAntiXray entity / hologram / drop occlusion
+                if (visibleToPlayer && dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.antixray.EntityVisibilityCheck.ENABLED.get()
+                    && !dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.antixray.EntityVisibilityCheck.isVisibleSync(player, this.entity)) {
+                    visibleToPlayer = false;
+                }
+                // SourbyCraft end - RayTraceAntiXray entity / hologram / drop occlusion
                 if (visibleToPlayer) {
                     if (this.seenBy.add(player.connection)) {
                         // Paper start - entity tracking events
